
  does a thing for the folder it is run in, and says what it changed

  USAGE


    app [command] [--flags]


  COMMANDS

    completion [command]  Generate the autocompletion script for the specified
                          shell
    help [command]        Help about any command

  FLAGS

    --accessible          Questions asked as plain lines for a screen reader
    --folder              The folder to work in, when it is not the one the run
                          starts in
    -h --help             Help for app
    --json                One JSON document on stdout, the rest on stderr
    --loud                Make noise about every file the run reads or writes,
                          one line each
    --no-color            No colour, as NO_COLOR asks
    --plain               No live view or pager, and questions as plain lines
    -v --version          Version for app
    --yes                 Answer yes to every question before a change
